_bg_color":"#2563eb","label_text":"Movement","label_color":"#e9d1b6","sublabel_text":"Harness design and fit can influence your dog’s natural movement.","stat_number":"66","stat_unit":"DOGS STUDIED","stat_color":"#e9d1b6","stat_font_size":46,"body_text":"<p>A study comparing three harness designs found significant differences in movement-related measures across 66 dogs.<\/p>","citation_text":"","show_button":false,"button_text":"SHOP FITNESS","button_link":"","button_text_color":"#e9d1b6","button_bg_color":"rgba(0,0,0,0)","button_border_color":"#e9d1b6","image_text_ratio":"40","border_radius":24,"border_width":0,"border_color":"#e5e5e5","bg_color":"#50332f","text_color":"#fffffe","shadow_enabled":false,"padding":28,"text_alignment":"left"}},"pillar_card_XJE8dP":{"type":"pillar_card","settings":{"icon_shape":"circle","icon_bg_color":"#2563eb","label_text":"Neck Pressure","label_color":"#e9d1b6","sublabel_text":"Walking equipment should be designed with comfort and pressure in mind.","stat_number":"83–832 kPa","stat_unit":"OF PRESSURE","stat_color":"#e9d1b6","stat_font_size":46,"body_text":"<p>A laboratory study of seven collar designs found pressure on a simulated dog neck ranging from 83 to 832 kPa under pulling forces.<\/p>","citation_text":"","show_button":false,"button_text":"SHOP RECOVERY","button_link":"","button_text_color":"#e9d1b6","button_bg_color":"rgba(0,0,0,0)","button_border_color":"#e9d1b6","image_text_ratio":"40","border_radius":24,"border_width":0,"border_color":"#e5e5e5","bg_color":"#50332f","text_color":"#fffffe","shadow_enabled":false,"padding":28,"text_alignment":"left"}},"pillar_card_8hxaMK":{"type":"pillar_card","settings":{"icon_shape":"circle","icon_bg_color":"#e9d1b6","label_text":"SAfEFTY","label_color":"#e9d1b6","sublabel_text":"Keeping pressure away from the neck can be especially important for sensitive dogs.","stat_number":"20","stat_unit":"Dogs Analyzed","stat_color":"#e9d1b6","stat_font_size":46,"body_text":"<p>In a 2025 study, collar